  "motivation": "Owner decision: Qwen through the Vercel AI Gateway is the default reply model. Before this, it only ran after hand-editing host.json, and turning a contact on still required a ready xcb subscription account even though Qwen wrote every reply.",
  "design": {
    "default": "default-reply-model.ts: with no habitat block in host.json, an admitted build runs the gateway writer (alibaba/qwen3.5-flash, credential file vercel-ai-gateway, $1/day, no evolution model, 1500ms debounce) once the key file exists owner-only. An explicit habitat block wins, including enabled:false. An unadmitted source daemon silently runs without the default instead of failing startup; an explicit block keeps the existing admission failure.",
    "key": "`textbutler providers gateway-key` reads the key from a pipe or private file through local-custody's protected input (terminals refused, never argv or environment), validates one printable token up to 4096 bytes, and publishes it atomically as mode 0600 in a 0700 directory. The key is never printed.",
    "enablement": "control-service enableAutomation skips agent-account model selection when a reply writer is active, because that writer classifies and composes every automatic reply; the agent capability reports available with the writer's model. Grants, contact settings and dispatch checks are unchanged.",
    "surfaces": "Readiness names the reply model or the one command to add a key; the TUI contact picker shows 'replies by Qwen 3.5 Flash (Vercel AI Gateway)'; contacts list JSON carries replyModel; help documents the command."
  },
